---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { sideGames } from '../lib/sideGames';
import { ROUND_FORMAT_COUNT } from '../lib/roundFormats';
import PoweredByStripe from '../components/payments/PoweredByStripe.astro';
import PlanCards from '../components/PlanCards.astro';
import PromoBar from '../components/PromoBar.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Pricing · Bagpipe Golf">
  <main class="pagewrap">
    {/* League plan (LEAGUE_SUBSCRIPTION_AND_PLAN_GATING_PLAN.md, flutter
         repo): $2,000 a year PER LEAGUE, card only, 12 months from the start
         date, renews yearly. Leagues that existed before the plan launched
         get 12 months free (plan L5/L9).
         Tournaments (Sam, 2026-10-25): free with a field of up to 36
         players "for now"; $240 per tournament at 37 or more (briefly $170 on 2026-10-30, back to $240 the same day). The threshold lives in
         billing.config, so this copy and that number change together.
         A tournament run inside a league is covered by that league's plan.
         llmsTxt.ts states the same figures — pricingCopy.test.ts keeps the
         two in step. */}
    <p class="pagewrap__eyebrow">Pricing</p>
    <h1 class="pagewrap__title">Free to play. Simple pricing to host.</h1>
    <p class="pagewrap__sub">
      Players never pay. Hosts pick the plan that fits, with no setup fee —
      and every league and club starts with a 30-day free trial.
    </p>

    {/* Plans (Sam, 2026-10-30): Single Event $240 (fields of 37+; free up
         to 36), League $2,140/yr = one league, ONE login, unlimited events/competitions/
         formats, plus a match-play companion league (Sam 2026-10-30, P7 in the
         Club plan; billing support is §3.8 — must ship before go-live). Club $2,970/yr for UNLIMITED leagues and up
         to 4 admin accounts (Sam 2026-10-30; was "up to 4 leagues" earlier
         the same day). League trial: 30 days, no card, ONE per
         director (api 20261115; shown once billing is enforced — until
         then nothing is locked, so it is saved). Club checkout is live (api #196) but set up by
         hand until the self-serve Club ships: admins each run their own leagues. Club trial (Sam 2026-11-04): 30 days,
         no card, granted by hand — an admin comps each of the club's leagues for
         30 days (POST /api/billing/admin/comp with ends_at). */}
    <PromoBar href="#plans" />
    <section id="plans" aria-label="Plans">
      <PlanCards />
    </section>

    <ol class="howbuy" aria-label="How buying works">
      <li><strong>Pick a plan.</strong> Every button above starts checkout for that plan.</li>
      <li><strong>Create your account and set up.</strong> Name your league or pick your event — about two minutes.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay by card on Stripe.</strong> Secure checkout, an emailed receipt, and your launch code already applied.</li>
    </ol>

    <p class="plans__players">
      <strong>Players are always free:</strong> the full scorecard, all
      {sideGames.length} side games, friends, spectator share, history and stats.
    </p>

    <section class="feeblock" id="league-plan-details">
      <h2 class="feeblock__h">How the league plan works</h2>
      <ul class="feeblock__list">
        <li>
          <strong>Try it free for 30 days.</strong> No card needed — set up
          your league, run your events, and subscribe any time before the
          trial ends to keep the season going. One free trial per organizer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>One league, one login.</strong> Run as many tournaments,
          competitions and formats inside it as you like. Running a season-long
          match-play series alongside your stroke-play season? That second league
          is included in the same plan.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>One plan covers one league for 12 months</strong> from the
          day you start it, and renews each year. Cancel any time and it runs
          to the end of the year you paid for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Paid by card</strong>, plus sales tax where it applies.
          You get an invoice, and you can update your card or download
          invoices any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Starting next season?</strong> Your plan moves to the new
          season's league — once a year — so you don't pay twice.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Already running a league on Bagpipe?</strong> It stays free
          for 12 months after the plan launches. We'll email you before
          anything changes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Smaller league?</strong> Discounted rates are available —
          <a href="mailto:hello@bagpipegolf.com?subject=Smaller%20league%20pricing">email hello@bagpipegolf.com</a>
          for details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Running several leagues?</strong> The
          <a href="#club-plan">Club plan</a> covers unlimited leagues, with up
          to 4 admin accounts, for $2,970 a year.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="feeblock__p">
        Without a plan, a league keeps what it already has — its current
        season, results and payments — but can't set up a new season, add
        tournaments, or start taking card payments.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* Competitor comparison (Sam, 2026-10-30). Every cell is what that
         company's OWN site says, read 2026-10-30, unless marked:
           GOLF GENIUS — golfgenius.com/products/tm: TM Club $1,425/yr +
             "$200 one-time onboarding fee"; TM Premium $4,275/yr + "$500";
             up to 36 holes. "League management" on both plans; "Mobile app
             with live scoring" and "Payment processing" PREMIUM-only.
             Side games: docs.golfgenius.com documents skins (basic,
             aggregate, team, optional), Nassau, Stableford, birdies/deuces,
             6/6/6 and more; no count published.
           BLUEGOLF — no public pricing; price/setup figures are as REPORTED
             by Live Tourney's Jan 2024 post (footnoted on the page).
             bluegolf.com/organizers: "registration & payment service",
             "Player of the Year / Order of Merit / Money List Standings".
             bluegolf.com/info/tdapp: Player App with optional live scoring.
             Side games: skins incl. aggregate, Cha Cha Cha, 3-2-1 (NCGA's
             BlueGolf TM Club feature sheet); no count published.
           LIVE TOURNEY — livetourney.com/pricing: Single Event $199, annual
             $2,700, Pro $3,900; "Registration Portals & Payments";
             "Extensive Game Library"; "Best for courses, league managers";
             its own FAQ: "How do players use Live Tourney if there is no
             app?" — web scoring, no app.
           UNKNOWN GOLF — unknowngolf.com/clubs-groups/pricing: custom
             quotes only. /clubs-groups/features: league software, season
             standings, in-app payments, Calcutta and pari-mutuel tools.
             iPhone + Android apps. /golf-wager-app: Skins, Dot/Trash,
             Banker, Vegas, Cash "and more", Venmo settle-up.
             /players/pricing: free membership; Unknown+ $49.99/yr or
             $14.99/mo unlocks custom side wagers ("Challenges").
         RE-READ 2026-11-07 (Sam: "more aggressive", check boxes): Golf
           Genius /products/tm unchanged — "Full library of tournament
           formats", no count; its marketing elsewhere claims the "widest
           variety" and "hundreds" of formats, so we DO NOT claim the most
           formats. Live Tourney /pricing unchanged ("Extensive Game
           Library", no count; FAQ "if there is no app"). BlueGolf
           /organizers: no side games or counts listed; branded iPhone and
           Android apps. Unknown Golf /clubs-groups/features: no count.
           The claim we make is the one we can prove: every game and format
           is NAMED on our site, and none of these publish a count.
         Never claim a rival LACKS something its site says it has. A cross
         only where the rival's own page says so; Premium-only or paid extra
         is "partly"; unknown is left blank. Re-read the sources before
         changing a cell and update the date below. */}
    <section class="feeblock" id="compare">
      <h2 class="feeblock__h">More games. Everything included. Less to pay.</h2>
      <p class="feeblock__p">
        Most golf event software makes you pay extra for the things players
        actually notice: the app, the side games, taking money. Bagpipe
        puts all of it in every plan, and gives players every game free.
      </p>

      <div class="bignums" role="list">
        <a class="bignum" role="listitem" href="/side-games">
          <span class="bignum__n">{sideGames.length}</span>
          <span class="bignum__l">side games, settled for you</span>
        </a>
        <a class="bignum" role="listitem" href="/tournaments#formats">
          <span class="bignum__n">{ROUND_FORMAT_COUNT}</span>
          <span class="bignum__l">tournament formats</span>
        </a>
        <div class="bignum" role="listitem">
          <span class="bignum__n">$0</span>
          <span class="bignum__l">for every player</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bignum" role="listitem">
          <span class="bignum__n">$0</span>
          <span class="bignum__l">setup fees</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="feeblock__p">
        <strong>Every one of them is named, with its rules, on this site.</strong>
        {' '}None of the platforms below publish how many side games or formats
        they have. Here are ours:
        {' '}<a href="/side-games">all {sideGames.length} side games</a> and
        {' '}<a href="/tournaments#formats">all {ROUND_FORMAT_COUNT} formats</a>.
      </p>

      <h3 class="compare__h">Price</h3>
      <div class="compare">
        <table class="compare__table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <td></td>
              <th scope="col">Annual price</th>
              <th scope="col">Premium</th>
              <th scope="col">Setup / onboarding</th>
              <th scope="col">Events</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="compare__us">
              <th scope="row">Bagpipe Golf</th>
              <td>$2,140 / year per league</td>
              <td>$2,970 / year (Club: unlimited leagues, 4 admins)</td>
              <td>Free</td>
              <td>Unlimited; single events free up to 36 players, $240 above</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Golf Genius</th>
              <td>$1,425 / year</td>
              <td>$4,275 / year</td>
              <td>$200; $500 for Premium</td>
              <td>Per facility, up to 36 holes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">BlueGolf<sup>*</sup></th>
              <td>About $2,000 / year</td>
              <td>$3,000 / year</td>
              <td>$500</td>
              <td>25 tournaments; unlimited on Premium</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Live Tourney</th>
              <td>$2,700 / year</td>
              <td>$3,900 / year (Pro)</td>
              <td>None listed</td>
              <td>Unlimited, or $199 per single event</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Unknown Golf</th>
              <td>Custom quote</td>
              <td>Custom quote</td>
              <td>Not published</td>
              <td>Not published</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="compare__h">Features</h3>
      <div class="compare">
        <table class="compare__table compare__table--ck">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <td></td>
              <th scope="col" class="compare__ushead">Bagpipe Golf</th>
              <th scope="col">Golf Genius</th>
              <th scope="col">BlueGolf</th>
              <th scope="col">Live Tourney</th>
              <th scope="col">Unknown Golf</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Side games, each named with rules</th>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y compare__uscell"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>{sideGames.length} games</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">No count published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">No count published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">No count published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">No count published</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Tournament formats, each named</th>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y compare__uscell"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>{ROUND_FORMAT_COUNT} formats</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">No count published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">No count published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">No count published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">No count published</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Side games settled for you: who owes whom</th>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y compare__uscell"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Every game</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">Not published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">Not published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">Not published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes, with Venmo</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Every side game free for players</th>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y compare__uscell"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Always</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">Not published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">Not published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">Not published</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--p"><span class="ck ck--part" aria-hidden="true">◐</span><span class="sr-only">Partly: </span>Custom wagers need Unknown+ ($49.99 / year)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">App scoring on the base plan</th>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y compare__uscell"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>iPhone and iPad (Android coming soon)</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--p"><span class="ck ck--part" aria-hidden="true">◐</span><span class="sr-only">Partly: </span>Premium only</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>iPhone and Android</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--n"><span class="ck ck--no" aria-hidden="true">✕</span><span class="sr-only">No: </span>Web only</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Card payments on the base plan</th>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y compare__uscell"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Dues and entry fees, to your own Stripe</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--p"><span class="ck ck--part" aria-hidden="true">◐</span><span class="sr-only">Partly: </span>Premium only</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">League management and season standings</th>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y compare__uscell"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes, plus a match-play companion league</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Season-long standings</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">No setup or onboarding fee</th>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y compare__uscell"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>Free</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--n"><span class="ck ck--no" aria-hidden="true">✕</span><span class="sr-only">No: </span>$200; $500 for Premium</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--n"><span class="ck ck--no" aria-hidden="true">✕</span><span class="sr-only">No: </span>$500<sup>*</sup></td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--y"><span class="ck ck--yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="sr-only">Yes: </span>None listed</td>
              <td class="ckcell ckcell--u">Not published</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="compare__key">✓ yes · ◐ partly or paid extra · ✕ no, per that company's own site · no mark: not published</p>

      <h3 class="compare__h compare__h--gap">Included in every Bagpipe price</h3>
      <ul class="feeblock__list checklist">
        <li><strong>No setup, onboarding or training fees.</strong> Create an event and send the invite.</li>
        <li><strong>A 30-day free trial for leagues</strong>, with no card needed.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Players never pay.</strong> The full scorecard, all
          {sideGames.length} side games with settle-up, and live
          leaderboards are free for every golfer in your field.
        </li>
        <li><strong>All {ROUND_FORMAT_COUNT} tournament formats</strong>, from scrambles and best ball to Stableford, match play and team cups.</li>
        <li><strong>The app, live scoring and card payments on every plan</strong>, not held back for a premium tier.</li>
        <li><strong>Leagues include their tournaments.</strong> Every event your league runs is covered by its plan.</li>
        <li><strong>Entry fees and dues go straight to you</strong>, through your own Stripe account.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="compare__note">
        Prices and features as published by each company, checked 7 November 2026:
        <a href="https://www.golfgenius.com/products/tm" rel="noopener">Golf Genius</a>,
        <a href="https://www.bluegolf.com/organizers/index.html" rel="noopener">BlueGolf</a>,
        <a href="https://www.livetourney.com/pricing" rel="noopener">Live Tourney</a> and
        <a href="https://www.unknowngolf.com/clubs-groups/features" rel="noopener">Unknown Golf</a>.
        Where a company does not say whether it offers something, we leave it unmarked rather than guess.
        <sup>*</sup>BlueGolf does not publish pricing; its price and setup figures are as reported by
        <a href="https://livetourney.com/blog/level-up" rel="noopener">Live Tourney in January 2024</a>.
        Plans and prices change, so check with each company before you decide.
        Golf Genius, BlueGolf, Live Tourney and Unknown Golf are trademarks of their respective owners.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* W6 — fee disclosure for hosts who collect money through us.
         Bagpipe's platform fee is 2% (F2, 2026-10-09; Sam re-confirmed
         2026-10-23), the same figure leagues/card-payments.astro shows.
         It is set per connected account (`merchant_accounts.
         application_fee_bps`, default 200), so this page states the
         number — keep the two pages in step if it ever changes. */}
    <section class="feeblock" id="collecting-money">
      <h2 class="feeblock__h">Collecting entry fees and dues</h2>
      <p class="feeblock__p">
        Optional, and off unless you turn it on. If you'd rather keep
        taking cash, Venmo or cheques, the roster has a
        <strong>Mark paid in cash</strong> button and nothing here
        applies to you.
      </p>
      <p class="feeblock__p">
        When you do collect by card, the money goes to
        <strong>your own Stripe account</strong>, not ours — you connect
        it once, Stripe verifies you, and payouts land in your bank on
        Stripe's schedule. We never hold your players' money.
      </p>
      <ul class="feeblock__list">
        <li>
          <strong>Stripe's processing fee</strong> comes out of each
          payment. Stripe sets it and publishes it at
          <a href="https://stripe.com/pricing" rel="noopener">stripe.com/pricing</a>
          — it's their price, not ours, and it's the same whether you
          use us or not.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Our platform fee is 2%</strong> of each card payment,
          taken before the money reaches you — on $50 dues that's $1.00.
          Your players see one total at checkout, never a line item for us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Refunds are yours to issue</strong>, from our roster
          or from your own Stripe dashboard. Either way the roster
          updates.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <PoweredByStripe />
    </section>

    {/* W7 — what connecting actually asks of a host, said BEFORE they
         start. Stripe's onboarding asks for a bank account, a tax id
         and a photo id; a host who meets that cold, three screens in,
         abandons it and tells us the feature is broken. */}
    <section class="feeblock" id="connecting-stripe">
      <h2 class="feeblock__h">Before you connect Stripe</h2>
      <p class="feeblock__p">
        Stripe — not us — has to verify who you are before it will move
        money for you. Worth having to hand:
      </p>
      <ul class="feeblock__list">
        <li><strong>A bank account</strong> for payouts.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>A tax ID</strong> — an EIN if the league is a legal
          entity, otherwise your SSN.
        </li>
        <li><strong>A photo ID</strong>, and your date of birth and address.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="feeblock__p">
        It takes a few minutes, and Stripe may take a day or two to
        finish verifying. You can set up your league and open sign-ups
        before it completes — only card payments wait.
      </p>
      <p class="feeblock__p">
        One person per league holds the Stripe login. Pick whoever keeps
        the books.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .howbuy {
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
    counter-reset: howbuy;
  }
  .howbuy li {
    counter-increment: howbuy;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .howbuy li::before {
    content: counter(howbuy);
    display: inline-grid; place-items: center;
    width: 22px; height: 22px; margin-right: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--brand-green); color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700;
  }
  .howbuy strong { color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .howbuy { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .card { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .card .chip { justify-self: start; }
  .card h3 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--brand-green-dark);
    margin: 6px 0 4px;
  }
  .card p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .card__per { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .plan { align-content: start; }
  .plan--featured { border: 2px solid var(--brand-green-dark); }
  .plan__lede { margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .plan__trial {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    color: var(--brand-green-dark);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
  .plan__list {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .plan__list li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .plans__players {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .feeblock { margin-top: 48px; }
  .feeblock__h {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--brand-green-dark);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .feeblock__p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .feeblock__list {
